  "raw_text": "No. If two files are truly byte-for-byte identical, a correct SHA-256 implementation will always produce the same digest.\n\nDifferent digests indicate that at least one of these is true:\n\n- The files differ in some bytes, possibly due to line endings, encoding, metadata embedded in the file, or trailing data.\n- Different data was hashed, such as a filename, archive metadata, or text-mode-transformed input.\n- The digest was displayed or encoded differently.\n- The hashing tool or hardware malfunctioned.\n\nFile-system metadata such as filename, permissions, and timestamps does **not** affect the digest when hashing only the file contents.",
